The `get_terms_orderby` filter in `get_terms()` doesn't get passed the `$maybe_orderby_meta` parameter.

If a plugin wants to use the `$maybe_orderby_meta` parameter when filtering the terms order, it must also filter `get_terms_args` and add the`$maybe_orderby_meta` argument to the `$args` array, so it can subsequently use it in the `get_terms_orderby` filter.

----

It would be additionally helpful to also pass `$orderby_raw` into the same filter, which would help plugin authors identify if `$orderby` had already been filtered or overridden.

----

Tangentially, the location of this filter is such that ordering by meta will always override it. A code comment says:

{{{
// Run after the 'get_terms_orderby' filter for backward compatibility.
}}}

...and I am sure that is the case, but I wonder if a back-compat break here would be fine, or whether maybe a newer, better filter at the end of that method would be best?

